  "about": "The repair state machine (repairs/state.ts) behind bookRepair, cancelRepair, approveRepairQuote, declineRepairQuote, adminUpdateRepair and adminSetRepairQuote. Ported from supabase/tests/repair_flow.test.sql, with the SQL in supabase/migrations/20261030000300_repair_flow.sql (the RPCs) and 20261028000100_auth_rls.sql (the booking policy and the 3-open limit). Staff steps: requested->confirmed->in_progress->ready->completed, or cancelled from any open step; the current status again adds only the note. in_progress and ready need an approved quote (QUOTE_NOT_APPROVED, detail: the quote status). Quotes while requested, confirmed or in_progress; each one waits for the customer again unless approved:true. Every change appends one events[] entry {status, quoteStatus?, quotePaise?, note?, by, byUid, at}. \"$repairId\" = the repairId bookRepair returned. \"expect\": {} means the call succeeds. Arrays in \"then\" match element by element and must have the same length ({} matches any element). In \"then\", null means the field is absent or null.",
